From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HID: usbhid: apply jspoll to gamepads too

usbhid.jspoll overrides the polling interval of devices whose top-level
collection is Generic Desktop Joystick, but most controllers declare
Gamepad (0x05) instead, so the parameter never reaches them.

The AYANEO Pocket VERT's built-in pad (4001:0428, Gamepad) asks for a
1 ms interval and answers every poll with the same report while idle:
~1000 xHCI interrupts a second on one core, which kept that core out of
its deep idle state most of the time (22% residency, 53% with the pad
unbound). Treat Gamepad like Joystick, so the device's boot arguments
and handheld-settingsd can set its rate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
 
 static unsigned int hid_jspoll_interval;
 module_param_named(jspoll, hid_jspoll_interval, uint, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(jspoll, "Polling interval of joysticks");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(jspoll, "Polling interval of joysticks and gamepads");
 
 static unsigned int hid_kbpoll_interval;
 module_param_named(kbpoll, hid_kbpoll_interval, uint, 0644);
@@ -1129,7 +1129,7 @@
 				hid->name, endpoint->bInterval, interval);
 		}
 
-		/* Change the polling interval of mice, joysticks
+		/* Change the polling interval of mice, joysticks, gamepads
 		 * and keyboards.
 		 */
 		switch (hid->collection->usage) {
@@ -1138,6 +1138,7 @@
 				interval = hid_mousepoll_interval;
 			break;
 		case HID_GD_JOYSTICK:
+		case HID_GD_GAMEPAD:
 			if (hid_jspoll_interval > 0)
 				interval = hid_jspoll_interval;
 			break;
